\f1 \cf2 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
The date in verse 1 of Ezekiel 31 is unambiguous enough. But immediately verse 2 gives us an interpretive challenge, even before we get to what Ezekiel is to say. First, there is Pharaoh, which would seem unambiguous enough, except that previous oracles addressed ostensibly to Egypt have had rhetoric aimed at the Jewish exiles in Babylon. But much more challenging is the second addressee. Multitude. Army. Crowd. Wealth. Splendor. Or, and this is strongly suggested by the way the word is used in chapter 30, hubris. Whichever way we read that word, it is the one belonging to or pertaining to Pharaoh. And how exactly we read that word seems intended to help us read the rest of this oracle.\
Which does not precisely get more straightforward as we move forwards. But I am curious what you think about the question Ezekiel is to open with.
